BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:pulitzer-center-global-south-civil-society-microgrants-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pulitzer Center: Global South Civil Society Microgrants 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Pulitzer Center funds civil society in the Global South to 
 build civic engagement projects around Pulitzer Center-supported journalis
 m: grassroots collectives\, community-led movements\, ARTISTS and civic co
 alitions taking published reporting to the communities it concerns. This g
 rant cycle is restricted to the Center's Climate and Environment topics: R
 AINFOREST (drivers of rainforest degradation\, the role of global markets\
 , finance and policy\, centring the rights and roles of Indigenous peoples
 )\, OCEAN (degradation of marine environments\, ocean health and the clima
 te crisis\, ocean governance\, science-backed and community-led solutions)
 \, and CLIMATE AND LABOR (the intersection of climate and labour\, includi
 ng gender\, livelihoods\, adaptation and community resilience). WHAT COUNT
 S AS A PROJECT: community engagement and organising that connects reportin
 g with audiences\; creative expressions\, explicitly including digital cam
 paigns\, public performances and creative publication formats\; public dia
 logues bringing together affected communities\, journalists\, decision-mak
 ers and academia\; and other innovative uses of the reporting that build o
 n local cultural practices. Every project must use at least one published 
 Pulitzer Center-supported reporting project meaningfully\, or involve a Pu
 litzer Center-supported journalist centrally\, and must name a clear targe
 t audience. OUT OF SCOPE: journalism and reporting projects themselves (th
 ose go to the Center's reporting grants)\, anything not built on Pulitzer 
 Center-supported reporting\, direct advocacy or lobbying\, campaigns endor
 sing political candidates or parties\, and for-profit projects. WHO CAN AP
 PLY: grassroots organisations\, community educators\, civil society organi
 sations and coalitions\, youth movements and other groups working at the i
 ntersection of journalism\, civic rights and active citizenship\, with pas
 t experience running civic engagement activities in the Global South\, pro
 ven experience on the named topics\, and the operational capacity to manag
 e a microgrant from an international organisation. APPLICATION: a project 
 description of no more than 400 words\, the target audience and desired im
 pact\, your methodology\, a timeline and budget\, the lead applicant's CV 
 with a letter of recommendation\, and\, where activities involve Indigenou
 s peoples or traditional communities\, a signed or recorded statement of c
 onsent from a community member. Applications are accepted in English\, Spa
 nish\, Portuguese\, French and Indonesian through Submittable. TIMELINE: a
 pplications 15 August to 6 September 2026\, selection announced mid-Septem
 ber 2026\, onboarding October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pulitzer Center\nLoca
 tion: Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and South
 east Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. Ci
 vil Society Microgrant instead.\nAward: USD 2\,000 to USD 4\,000 per proje
 ct. Applicants name the amount requested and submit a draft budget. Funds 
 are transferred to the partner after the agreement is signed\; partners fi
 le a financial narrative and outcomes report at the end but are NOT requir
 ed to collect detailed receipts. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to six 
 months of implementation\, October 2026 to March 2027\, with a virtual che
 ck-in in December 2026 and closure in early March 2027.\n\nMore: https://p
 ulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/global-south-
 civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://pulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/g
 lobal-south-civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and Sou
 theast Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. 
 Civil Society Microgrant instead.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-voucher-art-event-mexico-art-week-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Voucher Art Event\, Mexico Art Week 2027
DESCRIPTION:A Mondriaan Fund voucher sending visual artists to Mexico Art W
 eek 2027 in Mexico City\, built around the Zona Maco art fair. The voucher
  covers admission to the Zona Maco preview days\, a curated programme duri
 ng the week\, a networking event with the Dutch Embassy and hotel accommod
 ation from 2 to 7 February 2027\, plus a EUR 1\,300 contribution to travel
  costs. Fifteen vouchers are available. ELIGIBILITY: visual artists from t
 he Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom with at least one year
  of professional practice. Applicants may not be enrolled in a bachelor's\
 , master's or PhD programme\, with an exception for part-time programmes u
 nder 20 hours per week. CONDITIONS: the artist must be available to stay i
 n Mexico City from 2 to 7 February 2027 and take part in all scheduled act
 ivities\, and must submit a written evaluation after the visit. APPLY thro
 ugh the Mondriaan Fund online system with a CV (maximum three pages)\, a m
 otivation statement addressing your international ambitions\, the relevanc
 e of Mexico Art Week to your practice and your networking strategy\, bank 
 details and\, if applicable\, a BRP extract. Deadline 10 September 2026 be
 fore 16:00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan F
 und\nLocation: Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbea
 n part of the Kingdom. The event takes place in Mexico City\, Mexico.\nAwa
 rd: A voucher covering admission to the Zona Maco preview days\, a curated
  programme during Mexico Art Week 2027\, a networking event with the Dutch
  Embassy\, and hotel accommodation from 2 to 7 February 2027\, plus a EUR 
 1\,300 contribution towards travel costs. 15 vouchers are available. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Mexico Art Week 2027 runs 3 to 7 February 2027\;
  the artist must be available to stay in Mexico City from 2 to 7 February 
 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/v
 oucher-art-event-mexico-art-week-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/voucher-art-e
 vent-mexico-art-week-2027/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:Applicants must be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part 
 of the Kingdom. The event takes place in Mexico City\, Mexico.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-international-collaborative-projects-heritage-institutes-2026
 @artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: International Collaborative Projects with
  Heritage Institutes (September 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This scheme funds cultural heritage institutions in the Netherl
 ands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom that want to collaborate with f
 oreign heritage institutions on research projects in shared collection are
 as\, including art historical and provenance research. A development phase
  can also be funded\, covering travel\, accommodation and presentation cos
 ts while the collaboration is being shaped. CONDITIONS: the applicant inst
 itution must be publicly accessible and manage nationally significant cult
 ural heritage\; it must partner with comparable institutions abroad\; the 
 research must be presented by both the Dutch and the international partner
 s\; the applicant must contribute significantly to financing the project\;
  and the international partners' share of costs must be proportional to th
 e Mondriaan Fund grant. AMOUNTS: up to 40% of variable project costs for t
 he main project\, or up to 70% of variable costs capped at EUR 15\,000 for
  development research. APPLY through the Mondriaan Fund online application
  system after registering an account. Deadline 10 September 2026 before 16
 :00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time (an earlier 28 May 2026 round has pa
 ssed).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Applicant institutions m
 ust be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; the
  partner institutions are abroad.\nAward: Determined per application. Up t
 o 40% of variable project costs. For a development research phase\, up to 
 70% of variable costs capped at EUR 15\,000\, covering travel\, accommodat
 ion and presentation costs. The applicant must contribute significantly to
  the project financing\, and the international partners' cost share must b
 e proportional to the Mondriaan Fund grant. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Project-based research collaboration. Two annual rounds\; this card cover
 s the 10 September 2026 deadline.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/e
 n/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international-collaborative-projects-with-herit
 age-institutes/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international
 -collaborative-projects-with-heritage-institutes/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant institutions must be based in the Netherlands or the Car
 ibbean part of the Kingdom\; the partner institutions are abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-heritage-innovation-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Heritage Innovation (September 2026 round
 )
DESCRIPTION:Heritage Innovation funds projects and research tracks that con
 tribute to substantive innovation in the heritage sector. Examples given b
 y the fund include developing new narratives about cultural heritage\, str
 engthening regional collaboration across the sector\, redesigning how a co
 llection is presented\, and feasibility studies on technological applicati
 ons such as AI or gamification\, which makes this one of the more tech-adj
 acent Mondriaan schemes. WHO CAN APPLY: museums and collection-holding cul
 tural heritage institutions\, including archives\, in the Netherlands and 
 the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. Cultural organisations in the heritage 
 sector may also apply if they collaborate with one or more collection-hold
 ing institutions. All applicants must be non-profit\, not-for-profit entit
 ies. NOT FUNDED: fixed costs\, restoration\, building museums\, or regular
  operations. CONDITIONS: institutions must subscribe to the Fair Practice 
 Code\, the Culture Governance Code and the Diversity and Inclusion Code\, 
 and must pay visual artists fairly where artists are involved. AMOUNTS: pr
 ojects get up to 40% of variable project-related costs on a minimum projec
 t budget of EUR 25\,000\; research tracks get up to 70% of costs capped at
  EUR 15\,000 with no minimum budget. APPLY through the Mondriaan Fund onli
 ne system after registering an account. Deadline 17 September 2026 before 
 16:00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\n
 Location: Museums and collection-holding heritage institutions in the Neth
 erlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.\nAward: Projects: up to 40%
  of variable project-related costs\, with a minimum project budget of EUR 
 25\,000. Research tracks: up to 70% of costs\, capped at EUR 15\,000\, wit
 h no minimum budget. No application fee.\nDuration: Project or research tr
 ack. This card covers the 17 September 2026 deadline.\n\nMore: https://www
 .mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/heritage-innovation/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/heritage-inno
 vation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Museums and collection-holding heritage institutions in the Nether
 lands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sundance-collab-merrell-storytelling-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260818
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260819
SUMMARY:Deadline: Sundance Collab x Merrell: Brand-Supported Storytelling P
 rogram 2026
DESCRIPTION:Sundance Collab and Merrell are selecting five filmmakers from 
 around the world to each make an original 60 to 90 second vertical film fo
 r social platforms\, built around Merrell's 'It Starts Outside' brand plat
 form. The brief is not a commercial: it asks for a complete\, emotionally 
 resonant human story in which the outside acts as a catalyst for change\, 
 exploring how stepping outside is an antidote to increasingly screen-locke
 d\, indoor lives. Stories should reflect transformation (a moment of reset
 \, reconnection or personal shift)\, connection (belonging\, community\, r
 enewed relationship) and human truth (an observed\, emotionally grounded m
 oment). The strongest entries show what changed in a person because they w
 ent outside\, emotionally\, physically\, mentally\, creatively\, spiritual
 ly or psychologically\, rather than a final achievement. Selected filmmake
 rs enter a three-day online intensive in September on collaborating with a
  brand\, then receive USD 20\,000 to produce and deliver their greenlit co
 ncept\, cutdowns (:06\, :15\, :30) and stills between October and December
 \, with scheduled check-ins. One participant also receives a covered hotel
  stay to join the team at the Sundance Film Festival in January 2027. APPL
 ICATION: one entry per person\; all submitted materials must be created by
  the submitter\; all answers and materials must be in English or carry Eng
 lish subtitles. The core submission is a written response of up to 500 wor
 ds on how you would approach the brief. CRITICAL GUIDELINES: design for ve
 rtical with a strong hook in the first five seconds\; prioritise human\, o
 bservational storytelling over polished commercial aesthetics\; feature re
 al people and authentic moments\; treat the outside as context rather than
  the hero\; favour everyday\, intimate moments over epic outcomes\; avoid 
 overt brand narration\; no competitor products (Merrell product is provide
 d but must not be the focus)\; no AI-generated content in consumer-facing 
 materials. Selection criteria are originality\, emotional arc\, a distinct
  point of view and cultural relevance. TIMELINE: submissions opened 28 Jul
 y 2026\; deadline 11:59 p.m. PT on Tuesday 18 August 2026 (08:59 CEST on 1
 9 August)\; selected artists notified by 16 September 2026. An Insider Ses
 sion with Merrell Creative Director Alex Ho and Sundance Collab Director P
 atty West runs on 11 August. Sundance Collab provides accommodations and s
 upport services for participants with disabilities\; email accessibility@s
 undance.org to arrange services.\n\nOrganisation: Sundance Collab (Sundanc
 e Institute) in collaboration with Merrell\nLocation: Online program\, ope
 n to filmmakers worldwide. Production takes place wherever the filmmaker i
 s based. One participant receives a covered hotel stay at the Sundance Fil
 m Festival in Park City\, Utah\, USA in January 2027.\nAward: USD 20\,000 
 production budget per selected filmmaker to make and deliver the greenlit 
 concept\, cutdowns (:06\, :15\, :30) and stills. Includes an online brand-
 supported storytelling program\, and a covered hotel stay for one particip
 ant to attend the Sundance Film Festival in January 2027. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: Program runs September to December 2026\, with an online in
 tensive 30 September to 2 October 2026\, production in October\, post-prod
 uction in November and delivery by 14 December 2026.\n\nMore: https://coll
 ab.sundance.org/catalog/Merrell-Brand-Supported-Storytelling-Program?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://collab.sundance.org/catalog/Merrell-Brand-Supported-Storytellin
 g-Program?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online program\, open to filmmakers worldwide. Production takes pl
 ace wherever the filmmaker is based. One participant receives a covered ho
 tel stay at the Sundance Film Festival in Park City\, Utah\, USA in Januar
 y 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:knowcase-sonar-cotec-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260908
SUMMARY:Deadline: KNOWCASE Open Call 2027: permanent digital-culture instal
 lation in Madrid (Sonar+D x Fundacion Cotec)
DESCRIPTION:Fundacion Cotec (a Spanish innovation-focused non-profit) and S
 onar+D\, building on an initial experiment at Sonar 2026\, invite proposal
 s for a long-term installation at KNOWCASE\, the street-level showcase of 
 Cotec's Madrid headquarters in Chamberi\, visible to the public 24 hours a
  day. THEME: digital culture\, meaning projects that combine knowledge\, r
 esearch\, science and data with art\, technology and social impact. Cotec'
 s stated priorities are the big transitions (analogue to digital\, linear 
 to circular economy\, tangible to intangible) plus innovation ecosystems a
 nd R&D&I\, the climate crisis\, the future of work and learning\, social d
 ivides\, citizen participation and democratic health. WHAT YOU GET: a budg
 et of up to EUR 100\,000 plus VAT covering everything (design\, production
 \, installation\, maintenance\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, acc
 ommodation and insurance)\, and a minimum 24-month public display from Feb
 ruary 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artists\, collectives\, designers\, technologis
 ts\, universities\, research centres\, startups\, businesses\, creative ag
 encies\, producers\, cultural institutions and multidisciplinary teams\, i
 nternationally\; applicants must demonstrate solid experience and a releva
 nt portfolio. CONSTRAINTS: the proposal must be original and never previou
 sly exhibited\, must include participative or interactive elements\, must 
 encourage critical thinking\, and must be technically and financially viab
 le for the full 24+ month exhibition period (durability and maintenance ar
 e central selection criteria). Selection weighs conceptual quality highest
  (40 percent)\, followed by public interactivity (25 percent). HOW TO APPL
 Y: one PDF of maximum 15 pages containing summary\, concept\, technical pr
 oposal\, visuals\, budget\, timeline\, team profile\, portfolio and declar
 ation\, in Spanish\, another official language of Spain\, or English\, via
  the application portal linked from the terms and conditions. Results anno
 unced 14 October 2026. Deadline 7 September 2026 at midnight CEST.\n\nOrga
 nisation: Fundacion Cotec and Sonar+D\nLocation: Installation at the KNOWC
 ASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headquarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Sp
 ain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. The call is international\; appli
 cations accepted in Spanish\, other official languages of Spain\, or Engli
 sh.\nAward: Up to EUR 100\,000 (plus VAT)\, all-inclusive: conceptualisati
 on\, design\, technical development\, production\, installation\, maintena
 nce\, documentation\, artist fees\, travel\, accommodation and insurance.\
 nDuration: Installation displayed for a minimum of 24 months\, starting Fe
 bruary 2027\n\nMore: https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://sonar.es/en/news/knowcase-open-call-2027?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Installation at the KNOWCASE storefront of Fundacion Cotec's headq
 uarters in Chamberi\, Madrid\, Spain\, a street-level venue visible 24/7. 
 The call is international\; applications accepted in Spanish\, other offic
 ial languages of Spain\, or English.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-fine-art-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Fine Art Award 2027
DESCRIPTION:A one-year award enabling an emerging Indian visual artist to p
 ursue independent practice\, with a stipulation to attend a recognised art
  residency programme in India for four weeks during the year. ELIGIBILITY 
 IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens currently living in India\, born on or afte
 r 1 January 1996\, who are either recent graduates\, postgraduates or fina
 l-year students of a leading Indian visual arts institute\, or artists wit
 hout those formal credentials but with a record of exhibition participatio
 n. First-year MA students are not eligible. Awardees submit progress repor
 ts at six months and on completion\, plus documentation of the residency. 
 Applications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. Shortlisti
 ng is expected in late October 2026 with interviews in early November.\n\n
 Organisation: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to India
 n citizens currently living in India.\nAward: INR 300\,000 (around USD 3\,
 400 / EUR 2\,950) for one year\, plus a fully covered four-week art reside
 ncy at an Indian art institution. No application fee.\nDuration: Twelve mo
 nths of independent practice\, including a mandatory four-week residency w
 ithin India.\n\nMore: https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e1
 4093-df9b-41c5-af96-ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/75e14093-df9b-41c5-af96
 -ce2360e64e1b/the-inlaks-fine-art-award-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens currently living in India.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:inlaks-theatre-award-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation: Inlaks Theatre Art Award 20
 27
DESCRIPTION:A skill-enhancement award for emerging Indian theatre practitio
 ners\, supporting participation in recognised training workshops\, residen
 cies and similar programmes rather than the production of a specific work.
  ELIGIBILITY IS RESTRICTED: Indian citizens born after 1 January 1991\, wi
 th preference given to holders of a theatre degree from a leading Indian i
 nstitution. Recipients report at the six-month mark and on completion. App
 lications close 15 August 2026 at 23:59 IST via Submittable. The foundatio
 n runs several other awards on adjacent deadlines\, including the Inlaks-A
 ttakkalari Dance Studentship (30 August 2026) and a two-month Inlaks Resid
 ency at the International Center of Photography in the USA for emerging In
 dian photographic practitioners (31 August 2026).\n\nOrganisation: Inlaks 
 Shivdasani Foundation\nLocation: India. Open to Indian citizens.\nAward: I
 NR 15\,000 per month for up to 12 months\, around INR 180\,000 total (roug
 hly USD 2\,050 / EUR 1\,780). No application fee.\nDuration: Up to twelve 
 months of skill enhancement\, with six-month interim and final reporting.\
 n\nMore: https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.inlaksfoundation.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:India. Open to Indian citizens.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:musikfonds-outer-ear-2026-2@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Musikfonds: Outer Ear Special Programme (Round 2026/2)
DESCRIPTION:Outer Ear is Musikfonds' dedicated special programme for partic
 ipatory projects in experimental music\, and the strand that most cleanly 
 matches an experimental and sound-art public-programme brief rather than c
 oncert-series funding. It emphasises the creative process and audience par
 ticipation over finished works\, explicitly targeting audiences for experi
 mental music\, which makes it suitable for workshop-plus-presentation form
 ats\, listening programmes and process-led sound art events. Application w
 indows run twice yearly: 1 to 30 April 2026 (closed) and 1 to 30 October 2
 026\, the next live deadline. THE FIRST OUTER EAR ROUND WAS HIGHLY COMPETI
 TIVE\, with 14 projects approved at an 8.6 percent success rate\, so treat
  it as a long shot. As with all Musikfonds strands\, the applicant must be
  based in Germany\, projects abroad are ineligible\, and double-funding wi
 th BKM or with projects run by permanently institutionally supported bodie
 s is excluded. Note that Musikfonds' Small and Large Project Funding stran
 ds are listed separately in the Grant Desk\; Outer Ear is a distinct progr
 amme with its own window.\n\nOrganisation: musikfonds e.V.\nLocation: Germ
 any. Projects taking place abroad are excluded.\nAward: FLAG\, UNVERIFIED:
  per-project amounts are not published on the programme overview page and 
 must be confirmed via the application portal at musikfonds-antrag.de. No a
 pplication fee indicated.\nDuration: Project-based.\n\nMore: https://www.m
 usikfonds.de/foerderprogramme/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.musikfonds.de/foerderprogramme/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Germany. Projects taking place abroad are excluded.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-rotterdam-projectsubsidie-cultuur-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Rotterdam: Project Subsidy Culture (Projectsubsi
 die Cultuur\, September 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Rotterdam's standing project fund for one-off artistic and cult
 ural activity\, and the most accessible municipal route for festivals\, ex
 hibitions and public programmes in the city. The discipline list names e-c
 ulture outright alongside moving image and artistic film\, design and fash
 ion\, visual arts and photography\, architecture\, spoken word and all hyb
 rid forms\, so media-art and creative-technology programming is squarely i
 n scope. Both non-profit legal entities and natural persons may apply\, so
  individual artists are eligible. There is no published maximum per applic
 ation\; the real constraint is the EUR 272\,000 available per round agains
 t roughly 130 competing applications. Six rounds run every year with fixed
  closing dates on the first of January\, March\, May\, July\, September an
 d November. TIMING RULE: the activity may not start until eight weeks afte
 r the closing date of the round applied in\, so a 1 September 2026 applica
 tion supports activity from late October 2026 onward. Decisions normally a
 rrive within eight weeks of the round deadline\, extendable to 20 weeks. A
 ssociations and foundations apply via eHerkenning\, individuals via DigiD.
  Organisations already receiving Rotterdamse Culturele Basis\, Cultuurplan
 \, Impulsregeling\, national BIS\, Lokale Culturele Programmering or a CBK
  Rotterdam practice contribution are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Gemeente R
 otterdam (Municipality of Rotterdam)\nLocation: Activity must serve a Rott
 erdam interest and take place in or for Rotterdam. City-restricted by rele
 vance of the activity rather than by applicant address.\nAward: No stated 
 per-application cap. Annual pot EUR 1\,632\,000 split into six rounds of E
 UR 272\,000\, with roughly 130 applications per round. Discipline sub-caps
 : book writing max EUR 4\,500\; moving image R&D max EUR 4\,000\; moving-i
 mage production max EUR 12\,500\; post-production max EUR 4\,000. Applican
 ts must demonstrably seek other funds or sponsors. Awards over EUR 50\,000
  require an auditor's statement at reporting\, at the applicant's cost. No
  application fee.\nDuration: Single one-off project.\n\nMore: https://www.
 rotterdam.nl/projectsubsidie-cultuur-aanvragen?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.rotterdam.nl/projectsubsidie-cultuur-aanvragen?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must serve a Rotterdam interest and take place in or for 
 Rotterdam. City-restricted by relevance of the activity rather than by app
 licant address.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kunstraad-groningen-tweejarige-programmaregeling-2027@artificialnouveau
 .github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kunstraad Groningen: Two-Year Programme Scheme (Tweejarig
 e Programmaregeling\, 2027-2028)
DESCRIPTION:This is the Groningen scheme that actually funds festivals\, an
 d the correct counterpart to the Kunstraad's Projectenregeling\, which exp
 licitly excludes festivals and recurring programmes and redirects them her
 e. It supports coherent\, continuous public activity across 2027 and 2028 
 in all arts and heritage disciplines\, naming recurring production series\
 , festivals and programme lines as eligible\, with no exclusion of media a
 rt\, digital culture or experimental sound work. Annually recurring festiv
 als with a year-round paid organisation are explicitly named as eligible a
 pplicants. Awards run from EUR 5\,000 to 40\,000 per year against an annua
 l pot of EUR 325\,000\, capped at one third of total project costs\, so tw
 o thirds must come from municipal funds\, national funds\, box office or o
 wn contribution. Unusually\, the money may also be used to strengthen the 
 organisation itself on the business side\, not only to pay for programme c
 ontent. The application window is 1 July to 1 September 2026\, closing at 
 23:59\, and only applications received on time are processed. Applications
  must be submitted in Dutch via the Mijn Kunstraad portal with fair-pay st
 andards applied in the budget. Funding covers nothing before 1 January 202
 7. Professional non-profit organisations only\; amateur associations and i
 ndividual artists are directed elsewhere. Material investments\, equipment
  purchases and housing costs are excluded.\n\nOrganisation: Kunstraad Gron
 ingen\, on behalf of the municipality and province of Groningen\nLocation:
  Municipality and province of Groningen. The applicant organisation must b
 e based and active in Groningen. Region-restricted.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 min
 imum to EUR 40\,000 maximum per year across two years\, so up to EUR 80\,0
 00 total. Covers a maximum of one third of total project costs\, requiring
  roughly 67 percent co-financing. Annual scheme budget EUR 325\,000. No ap
 plication fee.\nDuration: Two years of programming\, covering 2027 and 202
 8.\n\nMore: https://kunstraadgroningen.nl/subsidies/tweejarige-programmare
 geling/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://kunstraadgroningen.nl/subsidies/tweejarige-programmaregeling/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Municipality and province of Groningen. The applicant organisation
  must be based and active in Groningen. Region-restricted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondspodiumkunsten-buitenlandse-voorstellingen-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds Podiumkunsten: Foreign Performances or Concerts in 
 the Netherlands (round 4\, 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Fonds Podiumkunsten's route for Dutch festivals and venues brin
 ging in exceptional foreign performing arts and concerts that Dutch audien
 ces would otherwise not see. The applicant must be a Netherlands-registere
 d legal entity running a venue or festival and carrying artistic and finan
 cial responsibility for its own programme\, so individuals and sole trader
 s cannot apply. Grants are calculated from travel and transport costs of t
 he incoming artists\, at a maximum of EUR 25\,000 per production and EUR 7
 5\,000 per applicant across several productions. The core test is that the
  foreign work is rarely or never seen in the Netherlands and substantially
  enriches the existing Dutch offer\, which favours experimental\, non-cano
 nical and cross-disciplinary programming over mainstream touring. Experime
 ntal music and sound-art programming is not excluded\; the selection crite
 rion is rarity and added value\, not genre. Applications go through the Mi
 jn Fonds portal and there is no fee. Four rounds run each year. TIMING: be
 cause the scheme competes against a shared EUR 267\,500 per-round pot and 
 assessment takes several weeks after the deadline\, organisers should appl
 y at least one full round ahead of the performance date and must not have 
 the activity already underway. Success rate in 2025 was 60 percent of 33 a
 pplications.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Podiumkunsten (Performing Arts Fund NL
 )\nLocation: Activity must take place in the Netherlands. Applicants from 
 Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Sint Maarten\, Saba and Sint Eustatius are als
 o in scope. No city or region restriction.\nAward: Maximum EUR 25\,000 per
  production\, capped at EUR 75\,000 for an applicant presenting multiple p
 roductions. Calculated on travel and transport costs of the foreign artist
 s and their production only. EUR 267\,500 available per round shared acros
 s this scheme and two sibling internationalisation schemes. Fees\, venue a
 nd production costs stay with the applicant. No application fee.\nDuration
 : Single performances or a short run of concerts within one programme or f
 estival edition.\n\nMore: https://fondspodiumkunsten.nl/subsidies/buitenla
 ndse-voorstellingen-of-concerten-in-nederland?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://fondspodiumkunsten.nl/subsidies/buitenlandse-voorstellingen-of-
 concerten-in-nederland?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:Activity must take place in the Netherlands. Applicants from Aruba
 \, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Sint Maarten\, Saba and Sint Eustatius are also in 
 scope. No city or region restriction.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-utrecht-projectsubsidie-cultuur-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Utrecht: Project Subsidy Culture (Projectsubsidi
 e Cultuur\, round 3 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Utrecht's main project fund for cultural activity with a public
  presentation in the city\, covering all art forms including experimental 
 and cross-disciplinary work. Individuals\, foundations\, associations and 
 companies are all eligible. Two bands apply: Category A of EUR 1\,000 to 5
 \,000 assessed on artistic importance and entrepreneurship\, and Category 
 B of EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000 which adds meaning for the city as a third crit
 erion. The activity must be exceptional or innovative\, or otherwise of va
 lue to the city\, its residents or the Utrecht cultural sector\; professio
 nal projects and amateur\, education or participation projects both qualif
 y. Three rounds run each year and the next closes 25 September 2026 at 17:
 00 CET. TIMING RULE\, which catches applicants out: for professional arts 
 applications the presentation may not take place earlier than 13 weeks aft
 er the round's closing date\, and for participatory applications the proje
 ct may not start earlier than 13 weeks after that date\, so a 25 September
  2026 application supports activity from late December 2026 onward. Decisi
 ons are issued no later than 13 weeks after the closing date\, following r
 eview by an independent Adviescommissie Projectsubsidies. Documentation is
  capped at 15 pages\, or 5 pages if a video is included. Applications go t
 hrough mijnsubsidie.utrecht.nl with DigiD or eHerkenning. Utrecht also run
 s a rolling Impulssubsidie Cultuur of up to EUR 2\,500 for first-time appl
 icants only\, open through 31 December 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Gemeente Utr
 echt (Municipality of Utrecht)\nLocation: Activity must have a presentatio
 n moment in Utrecht and benefit residents of the municipality of Utrecht. 
 City-restricted by presentation location\, not by applicant residence.\nAw
 ard: Category A: EUR 1\,000 to 5\,000. Category B: EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000. 
 No fixed co-financing percentage\, but a budget and coverage plan is manda
 tory. eHerkenning purchase costs may be included in the budget and are rei
 mbursed if awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Single project.\n\nMore
 : https://loket.digitaal.utrecht.nl/nl/producten/projectsubsidie-cultuur-a
 anvragen?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://loket.digitaal.utrecht.nl/nl/producten/projectsubsidie-cultuur-
 aanvragen?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must have a presentation moment in Utrecht and benefit re
 sidents of the municipality of Utrecht. City-restricted by presentation lo
 cation\, not by applicant residence.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bng-cultuurfonds-projectsubsidies-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: BNG Cultuurfonds: Project Grants (round closing September
  2026)
DESCRIPTION:BNG Cultuurfonds funds arts and culture projects that add value
  for Dutch municipalities and their inhabitants\, explicitly including tem
 porary exhibitions\, public programmes and festivals developed by professi
 onal makers. Media art\, digital culture and cross-disciplinary work quali
 fy as long as a professional maker's artistic vision leads the project. On
 ly stichtingen (foundations) may apply: no sole traders\, associations\, i
 ndividuals\, or foundations in formation. Applications go by email to aanv
 raag.cultuurfonds@bngbank.nl with a signed form\, a project plan of at mos
 t 3\,500 words\, a specified budget and coverage plan\, current statutes a
 nd a recent KvK extract. The grant is EUR 5\,000 to 15\,000 and can cover 
 no more than 35 percent of the budget. TIMING IS THE MAIN TRAP: for the 27
  September 2026 deadline\, feedback comes at the end of December 2026 and 
 the project may not start before 1 January 2027\, with applications for ea
 rlier-starting projects rejected outright with no exceptions. Missing docu
 ments are flagged up to one week before the deadline\, so anything submitt
 ed in the final week cannot be corrected. Plan for roughly four months of 
 lead time. Excluded: amateur art\, talent development\, education-focused 
 projects\, semi-permanent public art\, publications\, building or renovati
 on\, and regular operating costs. Further rounds: 3 January 2027\, 28 Marc
 h 2027\, 27 June 2027\, 3 October 2027 and 2 January 2028.\n\nOrganisation
 : Stichting BNG Cultuurfonds (BNG Bank)\nLocation: Project must take place
  in Dutch municipalities\; projects largely abroad are excluded. Not regio
 n-restricted\, but 2026 priority goes to Limburg\, Overijssel\, Drenthe an
 d Zeeland.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 minimum to EUR 15\,000 maximum. The request 
 must represent 5 to 35 percent of total project funding\, so at least 65 p
 ercent co-financing is required. The fund is never the sole financier\, an
 d place-specific projects require at least one local or regional co-financ
 ier. No application fee.\nDuration: Single project with a clear start and 
 end\; must be executed within two years of award. A grantee cannot reapply
  for 36 months.\n\nMore: https://www.bngbank.nl/bng-cultuurfonds/projectsu
 bsidies?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bngbank.nl/bng-cultuurfonds/projectsubsidies?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Project must take place in Dutch municipalities\; projects largely
  abroad are excluded. Not region-restricted\, but 2026 priority goes to Li
 mburg\, Overijssel\, Drenthe and Zeeland.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultuur-eindhoven-projecten-2027-r1@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven: Project Subsidy (Projecten\,
  2027 round 1)
DESCRIPTION:The mid-size project strand of Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven\, th
 e arm's-length body that distributes the city's culture budget\, and the m
 ain municipal route for an Eindhoven organisation to fund a festival\, exh
 ibition or public programme. Awards go up to EUR 35\,000 and cover a maxim
 um of 80 percent of eligible costs\, so at least a fifth of the budget mus
 t come from elsewhere. Unlike the Snelgeld strand this route is closed to 
 individuals: only private-law legal entities established in Eindhoven may 
 apply. Rounds run three times a year in fixed windows\; the next opens 1 S
 eptember and closes at 17:00 on 30 September 2026\, which is round 1 of th
 e 2027 cycle. TIMING: the decision lag is long by municipal standards at u
 p to 13 weeks after the submission window closes\, so a September 2026 app
 lication is decided around the end of December 2026 and activity should be
  planned for 2027. Given Eindhoven's design and technology profile\, media
 -art\, design and creative-technology programming fits the remit particula
 rly well. The parallel Snelgeld strand offers up to EUR 5\,000 on rolling 
 intake\, reopening 1 September 2026 and running until 31 December 2026 or 
 until the tranche budget is exhausted\, whichever comes first.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Stichting Cultuur Eindhoven\nLocation: Eindhoven. The applicant must
  be a legal entity based in Eindhoven and the activity must serve the Eind
 hoven cultural offering. City-restricted at the applicant level.\nAward: M
 aximum EUR 35\,000 per application and maximum 80 percent of eligible cost
 s\, so at least 20 percent co-financing is required. No application fee.\n
 Duration: Single project within the 2025-2028 policy period.\n\nMore: http
 s://cultuureindhoven.nl/informatie-over-subsidies-2025-2028/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://cultuureindhoven.nl/informatie-over-subsidies-2025-2028/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Eindhoven. The applicant must be a legal entity based in Eindhoven
  and the activity must serve the Eindhoven cultural offering. City-restric
 ted at the applicant level.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:gemeente-den-haag-kunst-cultuurprojecten-b-2026@artificialnouveau.githu
 b.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: Gemeente Den Haag: Arts and Culture Projects Category B (
 autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The larger of The Hague's two municipal project bands and the a
 ppropriate route for an organisation running a festival or substantial pub
 lic programme in the city. Awards range from EUR 10\,000 to 30\,000 agains
 t an annual ceiling of EUR 600\,000 for the whole strand. THE CO-FINANCING
  REQUIREMENT IS SEVERE and is the single most important planning constrain
 t: the municipal culture budget may fund at most 30 percent of the total p
 roject budget\, so an applicant seeking EUR 30\,000 must already have roug
 hly EUR 70\,000 secured or plausibly projected elsewhere. Only legal entit
 ies may apply\; individuals and informal collectives must use Category A i
 nstead (EUR 2\,000 to 10\,000\, 70 percent coverage ceiling\, next window 
 1 to 15 September 2026). Professional arts and culture organisations runni
 ng public projects in music\, theatre\, dance\, film\, literature\, visual
  arts or combinations are eligible. The next window opens 1 October and cl
 oses at 17:00 on 15 October 2026. TIMING: the decision term is 12 weeks af
 ter the window closes\, so an October 2026 application is decided around e
 arly January 2027 and activity should be scheduled from 2027 onward. Appli
 cations are handled through the municipality's subsidy system\, which migr
 ated to Easyfunders in April 2026. This scheme is independent of Stroom De
 n Haag. The underlying regulation runs to 31 December 2028.\n\nOrganisatio
 n: Gemeente Den Haag (Municipality of The Hague)\nLocation: The Hague. App
 licant must be active in Den Haag and the project must be publicly accessi
 ble there. City-restricted.\nAward: EUR 10\,000 to 30\,000 per application
 . The municipal culture-budget contribution may not exceed 30 percent of t
 he total project budget\, so at least 70 percent co-financing is required.
  Annual ceiling for the strand is EUR 600\,000. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: Maximum one year per project.\n\nMore: https://www.denhaag.nl/nl/subs
 idies/subsidies-cultuur-en-evenementen/subsidie-kunst-en-cultuurprojecten-
 aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.denhaag.nl/nl/subsidies/subsidies-cultuur-en-evenementen/su
 bsidie-kunst-en-cultuurprojecten-aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague. Applicant must be active in Den Haag and the project mu
 st be publicly accessible there. City-restricted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:norma-fonds-projectbijdrage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stichting NORMA: NORMA Fonds Project Grant (round 4\, 202
 6)
DESCRIPTION:The NORMA Fonds redistributes copyright remuneration collected 
 by Stichting NORMA into cultural\, social and professional projects involv
 ing performing artists\, and is one of the few Dutch schemes with four int
 akes a year and a genuinely short cycle. Both arts-sector organisations an
 d individual arts professionals may apply\, though the applicant needs a b
 ank account and legal footing and cannot be a BIS-funded institution. The 
 project must centre on performing artists in the copyright sense\, meaning
  people who perform a copyright-protected work: musicians\, dancers\, acto
 rs\, voice actors. This fits live experimental music\, sound performance a
 nd performative media-art work\, but not object-based exhibitions or non-p
 erformative installation programmes. The maximum grant is EUR 10\,000\, th
 e total project budget must stay under EUR 150\,000\, the applicant's annu
 al budget under EUR 500\,000\, and at least a quarter of the project budge
 t must be earned from audience income\, so this is a top-up rather than a 
 primary funding source. Budgets must honour NORMA's 2026 performer wage no
 rms. Applications are submitted online during a one-month window each quar
 ter\; the next round runs 1 to 30 October 2026\, closing at 23:59. TIMING 
 RULE: decisions arrive no later than eight weeks after the deadline\, and 
 the premiere date must fall at least eight weeks after the application dea
 dline. Organisations that already received a NORMA Fonds grant in 2024 or 
 2025 are excluded\, and supporting staff may not exceed 2 FTE.\n\nOrganisa
 tion: Stichting NORMA (collecting society for performing artists)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restriction s
 tated.\nAward: Maximum EUR 10\,000 per project. Total project budget may n
 ot exceed EUR 150\,000 and the applicant organisation's annual budget may 
 not exceed EUR 500\,000. At least 25 percent of the project budget must co
 me from audience or box-office revenue. Performer fees must meet the 2026 
 wage norms of EUR 139 per rehearsal and EUR 340 per performance. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: Single project\, typically a production or concert s
 eries. Final report due within six months of completion.\n\nMore: https://
 www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artificialnouveaug
 rantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stichtingnorma.nl/norma-fonds/aanvragen/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands-based arts-sector activity. No city or region restrict
 ion stated.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kulturstiftung-des-bundes-general-project-funding-2026@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260731
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260801
SUMMARY:Deadline: Kulturstiftung des Bundes: General Project Funding (Allge
 meine Projektfoerderung)
DESCRIPTION:Germany's flagship open\, non-thematic federal project line\, a
 nd one of the largest European funders that will back a festival\, exhibit
 ion programme or multi-partner convening run by an organisation rather tha
 n an individual artist. It funds large innovative projects across all arti
 stic fields\, explicitly including New Media alongside visual and performi
 ng arts\, music\, film\, photography and architecture. There is no publish
 ed maximum\, but the EUR 50\,000 minimum total project cost sets the scale
 \, and at least 20 percent co-financing is mandatory. Deadlines are twice 
 yearly at 12:00 CET: 31 July 2026 and 31 January 2027. TIMING RULE: decisi
 ons are made by an external jury meeting in May and November\, and no proj
 ect may start before its jury date\, so plan four to six months of lead ti
 me. Non-German organisations are genuinely eligible\, which is unusual at 
 this scale\, provided the project is visible in Germany and has an interna
 tional dimension. Two practical barriers: the application form must be com
 pleted in German\, and project communications must include a German-langua
 ge version.\n\nOrganisation: Kulturstiftung des Bundes (German Federal Cul
 tural Foundation)\nLocation: Activity must be visible to audiences in Germ
 any. Institutions headquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.\nAward: No
  fixed ceiling\, but total project costs must exceed EUR 50\,000 to be eli
 gible. The Foundation allocates up to EUR 10 million per year across this 
 line. At least 20 percent of total project costs must be secured from own 
 capital and/or third-party funding. No application fee.\nDuration: Project
 -length. Projects may not begin before the jury meeting.\n\nMore: https://
 www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_project_funding
 .html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.kulturstiftung-des-bundes.de/en/themes_focuses/general_proj
 ect_funding.html?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity must be visible to audiences in Germany. Institutions hea
 dquartered in Germany or abroad may apply.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:terra-foundation-collections-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: Terra Foundation for American Art: Collections Grants (20
 26 cycle)
DESCRIPTION:Funds organisations to reinstall permanent collections or mount
  temporary exhibitions drawn primarily from their own holdings\, on condit
 ion the project broadens understandings of American art and pursues inclus
 ive\, expansive curatorial practice. Planning grants of USD 25\,000 to 75\
 ,000 cover research\, advisory committees and conservation\; implementatio
 n grants up to USD 100\,000 cover interpretation\, exhibition design\, con
 servation\, public programmes and dissemination of research\, so the publi
 c-programming layer of an exhibition is fundable here. TIMING: the 2026 cy
 cle is two-stage\, with a grant inquiry due 3 August 2026\, a full proposa
 l for shortlisted applicants due 13 October 2026\, external panel review\,
  decisions in April 2027 and projects starting after 1 May 2027. That is a
  nine-month decision lag\, so this is planning-horizon money. Internationa
 l applicants are explicitly welcomed and need US 501(c)(3) status or the i
 nternational equivalent. The Foundation will not fund acquisitions\, equip
 ment\, exclusively online projects\, or projects consisting primarily of l
 oans. The American-art subject requirement is the main constraint for medi
 a-arts organisations.\n\nOrganisation: Terra Foundation for American Art\n
 Location: Worldwide. Museums\, art centres and community-based cultural or
 ganisations both inside and outside the US.\nAward: Planning grants USD 25
 \,000 to 75\,000 (conservation capped at 25 percent of a planning award)\;
  implementation grants up to USD 100\,000. No formal match\, but the Found
 ation prefers not to be sole funder. No application fee.\nDuration: Projec
 t-based\; funded projects start after 1 May 2027 following April 2027 deci
 sions.\n\nMore: https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-progr
 am/collections-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
URL:https://www.terraamericanart.org/what-we-offer/grant-program/collection
 s-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide. Museums\, art centres and community-based cultural orga
 nisations both inside and outside the US.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-exhibition-support-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Exhibition Support (Fall 2026 rou
 nd)
DESCRIPTION:Supports solo\, two-person and thematic group exhibitions of co
 ntemporary visual art. The Foundation explicitly prioritises artists whose
  work is under-recognised and whose practices are experimental or hard to 
 categorise\, which makes it a genuine route for media arts\, digital cultu
 re and art-and-science exhibitions rather than a blue-chip-only fund. Gran
 ts of USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 cover direct exhibition costs including arti
 st fees\, new commissions\, catalogue production and artist-designed publi
 c programming\, but not staff salaries. Applicants may request no more tha
 n 25 percent of total direct costs. The proposal is a roughly three-page c
 uratorial letter plus detailed direct-cost budget\, organisational budget 
 and IRS documentation. Deadlines are 1 March and 1 September annually\, wi
 th notifications 1 July and 1 January. IMPORTANT: this is a postmark or em
 ail-timestamp deadline\, not a portal deadline. Fiscal sponsors are explic
 itly not accepted\; the applicant must hold its own IRS ruling letter. The
  six-month-to-two-year timing rule is strict\, so a September 2026 applica
 tion suits exhibitions programmed from mid-2027 onward.\n\nOrganisation: T
 he Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visual Arts\nLocation: Applicant's own v
 enue. US-based 501(c)(3) required\; international organisations must first
  submit a letter of inquiry before any proposal is accepted.\nAward: USD 6
 0\,000 to 100\,000. Direct costs only (artist payments\, catalogue and pub
 lication\, artist-designed public programmes)\; staff salaries excluded. R
 equest must not exceed 25 percent of total direct project costs\, which fu
 nctions as a de facto 75 percent co-financing requirement. No application 
 fee.\nDuration: Exhibition must open between 6 months and 2 years after no
 tification.\n\nMore: https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guide
 lines/exhibition-support/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/exhibition-s
 upport/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant's own venue. US-based 501(c)(3) required\; international
  organisations must first submit a letter of inquiry before any proposal i
 s accepted.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-multiyear-program-support-2026@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Multi-year Program Support (Fall 
 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This is the closest thing in US foundation philanthropy to core
  support for an organisation running an ongoing public programme\, as oppo
 sed to a single exhibition. It funds a two-year slate of exhibitions\, res
 idencies\, public art\, screenings\, performances\, lectures and publicati
 ons\, which means a recurring festival or convening series can be underwri
 tten here. Grants are USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 over two years and may not e
 xceed 25 percent of annual operating budget. The Foundation states a prefe
 rence for organisations supporting artists with experimental\, hard-to-cat
 egorise practices\, putting digital culture\, sound art and art-and-scienc
 e programmers squarely in scope. Applications require a forward programme 
 schedule covering at least the twelve months after the award\, a three-pag
 e narrative focused specifically on how artists benefit (the stated centra
 l evaluation criterion)\, a full one-year organisational budget and 501(c)
 (3) documentation. Deadlines are 1 March and 1 September\, notifications 1
  July and 1 January. Fiscal sponsors are not accepted. Organisations that 
 received a Multi-year grant within the past year are ineligible\, and prop
 osals centred on anniversaries\, relocations or major renovations are expl
 icitly discouraged.\n\nOrganisation: The Andy Warhol Foundation for the Vi
 sual Arts\nLocation: Programming delivered by the applicant organisation. 
 US 501(c)(3) required\; international organisations must submit a letter o
 f inquiry first.\nAward: USD 60\,000 to 100\,000 across two years. Request
  must not exceed 25 percent of the organisation's annual operating budget.
  No formal match\, but the 25 percent cap means the balance must come from
  elsewhere. No application fee.\nDuration: Two years of programming\, begi
 nning after the 1 January 2027 notification.\n\nMore: https://warholfounda
 tion.org/grants/application-guidelines/multi-year-program-support/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/multi-year-p
 rogram-support/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Programming delivered by the applicant organisation. US 501(c)(3) 
 required\; international organisations must submit a letter of inquiry fir
 st.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:warhol-foundation-small-scale-project-grants-2026@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Andy Warhol Foundation: Project Grants for Small-Scale Or
 ganizations (Fall 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Launched in February 2026 as an expansion of the Foundation's p
 rogramme to reach organisations too small for the Exhibition Support and M
 ulti-year strands\, and it is the single most relevant new US scheme for s
 mall media-arts festivals. It funds visual arts projects with a public com
 ponent\, explicitly naming film festivals\, exhibitions\, installations\, 
 residencies and interdisciplinary collaborations. Grants are USD 20\,000 t
 o 30\,000 toward direct costs. The hard gate is the USD 200\,000 annual op
 erating budget ceiling plus US 501(c)(3) status held directly by the appli
 cant\, not via a fiscal sponsor. The Foundation states it assesses creativ
 e risk-taking and the growth of participating artists rather than communit
 y impact metrics\, which suits experimental sound and digital culture prog
 ramming. Proposals are a maximum of three pages plus a one-year operating 
 budget\, a project budget and IRS documentation. Deadlines are 1 March (pr
 ojects begin 1 July or later) and 1 September (projects begin 1 January or
  later). Youth-focused projects are ineligible. One project per round\, an
 d grantees must wait a year after project completion and final reporting b
 efore reapplying.\n\nOrganisation: The Andy Warhol Foundation for the Visu
 al Arts\nLocation: Applicant's own venue or programme\, with a mandatory p
 ublic component. US-based only.\nAward: USD 20\,000 to 30\,000 toward dire
 ct costs such as artist payments and production. No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Project must complete within one year of notification\; September-ro
 und projects may begin 1 January 2027 or later.\n\nMore: https://warholfou
 ndation.org/grants/application-guidelines/project-grants-for-small-scale-o
 rganizations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://warholfoundation.org/grants/application-guidelines/project-gran
 ts-for-small-scale-organizations/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant's own venue or programme\, with a mandatory public compo
 nent. US-based only.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-australia-arts-projects-organisations-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Australia: Arts Projects for Organisations (Sept
 ember 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Creative Australia's principal open-round project grant for art
 s organisations and the most directly relevant Australian scheme for mount
 ing festivals\, exhibitions and public programmes. The guidelines explicit
 ly list festivals\, productions\, exhibitions\, performances\, touring\, p
 ublishing\, recording\, collaborations\, research and community engagement
  as supported activity. Organisations may propose either a single project 
 or an entire programme of projects\, which can extend to a full artistic p
 rogramme for a given calendar year or longer\, so this can function as de 
 facto annual programme funding. The category is artform-agnostic and routi
 nely supports media arts\, digital culture\, experimental sound and art-an
 d-science work\; activity delivered online is explicitly permitted. NOTABL
 E: international organisations are eligible where the project demonstrably
  benefits practising Australian artists\, their work\, or Australian audie
 nces\, so a non-Australian festival can apply if it is programming Austral
 ian artists. The applicant must be a legally constituted entity: incorpora
 ted association\, company limited by guarantee\, or government statutory a
 uthority. Registration in the Application Management System must be comple
 ted at least one business day before the closing date. The round closes 1 
 September 2026 at 3pm AEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Australia\nLocation:
  Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationally\, o
 r online.\nAward: AUD 20\,000 to 100\,000. No matching or co-financing req
 uirement. No application fee. Organisational administrative costs should g
 enerally not exceed 10 percent of the total project budget or the applicat
 ion becomes less competitive.\nDuration: Activity must last no longer than
  two years from the proposed start date\; the project must commence after 
 notification and within one year of it.\n\nMore: https://creative.gov.au/i
 nvestments-opportunities/arts-projects-organisations?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunities/arts-projects-organis
 ations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationa
 lly\, or online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ernst-von-siemens-musikstiftung-project-funding-2026@artificialnouveau.
 github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Deadline: Ernst von Siemens Musikstiftung: Project Funding (October
  2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:One of the largest private funders of contemporary and new musi
 c in Europe\, and it funds the organising side of the field rather than in
 dividual artists\, which makes it directly usable by festivals. Eligible a
 ctivity includes festivals\, world premieres and revivals\, composition co
 mmissions\, events\, academies and workshops\, education projects\, sympos
 ia and musicological publications. Experimental and contemporary sound pro
 gramming is the core remit\; this is not a classical-repertoire fund. Ther
 e are two annual deadlines: 1 October at 14:00 CEST for projects starting 
 the following year with decisions by year-end\, and 1 March for projects s
 tarting in July or later with decisions by end of June. Grant sizes are no
 t published\, and the Foundation aims funding at artistic rather than over
 head costs. Only the organising institution may apply and only legal entit
 ies qualify: cultural institutions\, orchestra managers\, festival organis
 ers and ensembles. Self-applications and applications from individuals are
  explicitly refused. VOLUME LIMITS are strict and worth planning around: e
 ach institution may submit one application per deadline\, may be supported
  for only one project per year\, and may be supported for a maximum of thr
 ee projects across three consecutive years.\n\nOrganisation: Ernst von Sie
 mens Musikstiftung\nLocation: International\, no stated country restrictio
 n on the organising institution\, though the Foundation is Swiss and Germa
 n in orientation and administration.\nAward: No published minimum or maxim
 um. Primarily covers artistic costs\, not overheads. The Foundation explic
 itly will not fully fund a project\, and requires at least one other insti
 tution to participate financially at a level similar to the amount request
 ed\, functioning as a de facto 1:1 match. No application fee.\nDuration: P
 roject-based. The October deadline covers projects beginning the following
  calendar year.\n\nMore: https://evs-musikstiftung.ch/en/project-funding/a
 pplication/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://evs-musikstiftung.ch/en/project-funding/application/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International\, no stated country restriction on the organising in
 stitution\, though the Foundation is Swiss and German in orientation and a
 dministration.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-wales-festivals-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260730
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Wales: Festivals (2026 rounds)
DESCRIPTION:Festivals is one of the new National Lottery programmes Arts Co
 uncil of Wales launched on 13 April 2026\, and it is the clearest organisa
 tion-facing route for funding a public festival in Wales. It supports focu
 sed\, time-limited festivals delivering high-quality arts programmes to br
 oad audiences\, in a single artform or mixed artforms\, with preference gi
 ven to festivals that commission\, create and present new artistic work. G
 rants run GBP 500 to 100\,000 across four tiers\, with the tier ceiling ti
 ed to how long the festival has been established. Match funding is mandato
 ry: the Council covers at most 75 percent of eligible costs and in-kind su
 pport is capped at 10 percent. There are two deadlines in 2026\, both at 1
 pm: Wednesday 29 July 2026 and Wednesday 16 December 2026. TIMING RULE: a 
 minimum of twelve working weeks must fall between the deadline and the pro
 ject start date\, so activity applied for in the July round cannot begin b
 efore roughly late October 2026. Retrospective costs are ineligible. Indiv
 idual artists cannot apply.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Council of Wales\nLocati
 on: Festival must take place in Wales and demonstrate cultural value to th
 e local community. Welsh language integration expected.\nAward: GBP 500 to
  100\,000 across four tiers: Small up to GBP 10\,000\; Large up to GBP 35\
 ,000 (1+ year track record)\; Large up to GBP 60\,000 (3+ years\, regional
  significance\, 2+ day programme)\; Large up to GBP 100\,000 (5+ years\, n
 ational significance). Co-financing mandatory: the Council funds a maximum
  of 75 percent of eligible costs\, so at least 25 percent of project incom
 e must come from non-Arts Council and non-Lottery sources\, of which no mo
 re than 10 percent may be in-kind. No application fee.\nDuration: One or t
 wo years of festival activity\; two-year applications require a track reco
 rd and development plan.\n\nMore: https://arts.wales/festivals-0?utm_sourc
 e=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.wales/festivals-0?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
LOCATION:Festival must take place in Wales and demonstrate cultural value t
 o the local community. Welsh language integration expected.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arts-council-wales-create-and-engage-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260729
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260730
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Wales: Create and Engage (2026 rounds)
DESCRIPTION:Create and Engage is Arts Council of Wales's general-purpose Na
 tional Lottery programme for making and presenting arts work\, launched al
 ongside Festivals in April 2026\, and is the natural fit for exhibitions\,
  public programmes\, touring and participatory events that are not structu
 red as a festival. It funds creation\, presentation\, programming\, tourin
 g\, community participation and\, for organisations only\, professional de
 velopment. Small awards go up to GBP 10\,000 and large awards run GBP 10\,
 001 to 60\,000\, with up to GBP 100\,000 possible in exceptional cases wit
 h advance manager approval. At least 10 percent of project costs must come
  from non-Council\, non-Lottery sources\, a notably lighter co-financing b
 urden than the Festivals fund's 25 percent. TIMING RULES: Small Create and
  Engage is rolling with no set deadlines but requires a minimum of 10 work
 ing weeks between submission and project start\; Large Create and Engage h
 as fixed 1pm deadlines on 29 July 2026\, 30 September 2026 and 16 December
  2026\, with a minimum of 12 working weeks between deadline and project st
 art. WHO CAN APPLY: both organisations and individuals\, though individual
  applicants must be based in Wales. Non-UK organisations can participate a
 s partners but cannot lead. Applicants cannot have an application in to mo
 re than one Arts Council fund at the same time.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Coun
 cil of Wales\nLocation: Projects must take place mainly in Wales. Individu
 al applicants must be Wales-based\; organisations outside the UK may take 
 part as partners provided a UK-based eligible organisation leads.\nAward: 
 Small awards up to GBP 10\,000\; Large awards GBP 10\,001 to 60\,000\; exc
 eptionally up to GBP 100\,000 with prior approval from an Arts Council man
 ager. At least 10 percent of project costs must come from non-Arts Council
  and non-Lottery sources. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-length\; 
 activity must not already be underway at the point of application.\n\nMore
 : https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/create-and-engage?utm_source=arti
 ficialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://arts.wales/funding/individuals/create-and-engage?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Projects must take place mainly in Wales. Individual applicants mu
 st be Wales-based\; organisations outside the UK may take part as partners
  provided a UK-based eligible organisation leads.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:acni-aidf-organisations-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Deadline: Arts Council of Northern Ireland: Artists' International 
 Development Fund for Organisations (2026)
DESCRIPTION:The Artists' International Development Fund (Organisations) is 
 Arts Council of Northern Ireland's route for NI-based arts organisations t
 o take a first substantive step into international working. It is the orga
 nisations counterpart to the individual-artist AIDF under the Support for 
 the Individual Artist Programme\, which is a separate scheme with its own 
 amount band. Grants run GBP 1\,000 to 7\,000 and cover art materials\, res
 idency costs\, travel including airfare and mileage\, artistic and technic
 al fees for production or post-production\, venue hire\, and equipment cap
 ped at 50 percent of the request value. The deadline is Thursday 30 July 2
 026 at 12:00 noon\, and the online system closes precisely at noon. Applic
 ants must be NI-based\, must have received recognition for their work ther
 e\, and must not already have extensive international experience. The appl
 ication must evidence genuine interest from an overseas partner or host\, 
 so a confirmed international invitation\, residency offer or presentation 
 opportunity is effectively a precondition.\n\nOrganisation: Arts Council o
 f Northern Ireland\nLocation: Applicant organisations must be based in Nor
 thern Ireland\; the funded activity takes place internationally\, with an 
 overseas partner or host.\nAward: GBP 1\,000 to 7\,000. Covers art materia
 ls\, residency costs\, travel (mileage at 25.7p per mile plus airfare)\, a
 rtistic and technical fees for production or post-production\, venue hire\
 , project equipment capped at 50 percent of the request value\, and IT equ
 ipment up to GBP 1\,200 for laptops or GBP 500 for tablets. No application
  fee.\nDuration: Short\, early-stage international development activity.\n
 \nMore: https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-organisations/artists-inter
 national-development-fund-organisations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artscouncil-ni.org/funding-for-organisations/artists-internatio
 nal-development-fund-organisations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant organisations must be based in Northern Ireland\; the fu
 nded activity takes place internationally\, with an overseas partner or ho
 st.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bfi-national-lottery-discovery-feature-funding-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260814
SUMMARY:Deadline: BFI National Lottery Discovery Feature Funding (Debut Fic
 tion Features)
DESCRIPTION:Discovery is the debut-director production strand of the BFI Fi
 lmmaking Fund\, awarding up to GBP 1 million towards fiction features budg
 eted between GBP 1 million and GBP 3.5 million. It backs first-time featur
 e directors working alongside experienced producers\, and is structured so
  creative risk sits with a team rather than a lone filmmaker. ELIGIBILITY:
  applications must be made through a limited company registered and centra
 lly managed in the UK\, so unincorporated individuals cannot apply. A dedi
 cated lead producer with an established track record must submit\, and tha
 t producer must be someone other than the writer or director. The director
  must be making their first fiction feature\, meaning no prior feature at 
 or above a GBP 1 million budget and no prior commercial UK or Ireland thea
 trical distribution of a fiction feature. At least two people must be cred
 ited across the writer\, producer and director roles\, all aged 18 or over
  and not in full-time education. Projects need a fully developed script an
 d a runtime of at least 70 minutes. LIMITS: one application per production
  company\, producer and director per round\, and applications must arrive 
 at least 20 weeks before the proposed first day of principal photography. 
 ROUNDS: Round 2 closes at 5pm on Thursday 13 August 2026. Round 3 opens Th
 ursday 12 November 2026 and closes Wednesday 16 December 2026. Successful 
 applicants must publicly credit BFI National Lottery support.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: British Film Institute (BFI Filmmaking Fund\, National Lottery)\nLoca
 tion: United Kingdom (applications must come from a limited company regist
 ered and centrally managed in the UK)\nAward: Up to GBP 1\,000\,000 of Nat
 ional Lottery funding towards a fiction feature with a production budget b
 etween GBP 1\,000\,000 and GBP 3\,500\,000. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Single production award\; apply at least 20 weeks before the first day of
  principal photography. Decisions in principle within roughly 12 weeks of 
 the round closing.\n\nMore: https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/cre
 ate-films-tv-or-new-formats-storytelling/bfi-filmmaking-fund-discovery-imp
 act-feature-funding?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/create-films-tv-or-new-forma
 ts-storytelling/bfi-filmmaking-fund-discovery-impact-feature-funding?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United Kingdom (applications must come from a limited company regi
 stered and centrally managed in the UK)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bfi-national-lottery-creative-challenge-fund-round-2-2026@artificialnou
 veau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260922
SUMMARY:Deadline: BFI National Lottery Creative Challenge Fund (Round Two)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Challenge Fund does not fund films directly. It fu
 nds the organisations that run project-development programmes for UK creat
 ives working on narrative\, documentary or animation features\, or on narr
 ative immersive media projects. The BFI's stated aim is to decentralise de
 velopment away from a small number of London-centric gatekeepers and build
  a wider\, more resilient ecosystem of talent-development providers across
  the UK\, with a recently added emphasis on independent producers. ELIGIBI
 LITY: only legally constituted UK-based organisations may apply. Individua
 l filmmakers seeking development money should look to the BFI Filmmaking F
 und's Development strand instead. TIMING: Round One closed in March 2026 a
 nd has made its first awards. Round Two closes Monday 21 September 2026\, 
 with funded programme activity required to begin between 1 January and 30 
 June 2027. NOTE: award amounts are not published on the fund page. Success
 ful applicants must prominently credit BFI National Lottery support.\n\nOr
 ganisation: British Film Institute (BFI National Lottery)\nLocation: Unite
 d Kingdom (UK-based organisations running development programmes for UK cr
 eatives)\nAward: Award amounts are not published on the fund page. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Funded programme activity must start between 1 Jan
 uary and 30 June 2027 and\, in most cases\, be delivered within 12 months 
 unless the applicant is running multiple editions.\n\nMore: https://www.bf
 i.org.uk/get-funding-support/create-films-tv-or-new-formats-storytelling/b
 fi-national-lottery-creative-challenge-fund?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.bfi.org.uk/get-funding-support/create-films-tv-or-new-forma
 ts-storytelling/bfi-national-lottery-creative-challenge-fund?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:United Kingdom (UK-based organisations running development program
 mes for UK creatives)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:arm-holding-commission-h-residence-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260725
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260726
SUMMARY:Deadline: A.R.M. Holding / Art Dubai Projects: H Residence Sculptur
 e Park Commission (Dubai)
DESCRIPTION:A.R.M. Holding and HUNA\, with the commission supported and man
 aged by Art Dubai Projects\, invite artists to propose a permanent public 
 artwork for the H Residence Sculpture Park in Dubai\, the anchor piece of 
 the park's programme. Artists respond to the theme 'We Emerge Stronger tha
 n Before' through a permanent\, site-specific outdoor sculpture\; the stro
 ngest proposals will find what the phrase opens up (continuity\, endurance
 \, renewal\, collective presence\, the long view) through material\, form\
 , scale and the conditions of the site. Where language or text is incorpor
 ated\, Arabic should lead. TECHNICAL: footprint minimum around 15 sqm\, up
  to 3 m high\; weight restriction 5.5 kN/m2\; must be suitable for long-te
 rm outdoor display in Dubai (summer over 40 C\, humidity to 90 percent\, a
 bout six hours direct sun daily)\; presence by day and night. ELIGIBILITY:
  open to artists with or without gallery representation\; UAE-based\, regi
 onal and international artists welcome\; prior experience with permanent o
 r large-scale outdoor/public installation required. BUDGET: AED 1\,000\,00
 0 all-inclusive\; shortlisted artists receive full budget parameters and p
 roposal fees at the proposal development stage. SUBMISSION: CV and portfol
 io (attention to outdoor\, large-scale or permanent commissions)\, concept
  statement (max 300 words)\, a render or visualisation in context plus at 
 least one sketch\, technical specifications\, and a site response. TIMELIN
 E: submissions close 25 July 2026\; shortlist notified from 10 August\; co
 mmission awarded after September proposal development\; work unveiled at H
  Residence on 2 December 2026. Local fabrication strongly preferred. Quest
 ions: Shahad@artdubai.ae.\n\nOrganisation: A.R.M. Holding / HUNA / Art Dub
 ai Projects\nLocation: H Residence Sculpture Park\, Dubai\, UAE. Open to U
 AE-based\, regional and international artists.\nAward: AED 1\,000\,000 com
 mission envelope\, inclusive of artist fee\, design development\, fabricat
 ion\, materials\, production\, transport\, installation\, lighting and fin
 ishing. Proposal fees are available for shortlisted artists. No submission
  fee.\nDuration: Proposal development September 2026\; fabrication autumn 
 2026\; unveiling 2 December 2026\n\nMore: https://www.artdubai.ae/wp-conte
 nt/uploads/2026/06/ADP_ARM-HOLDING-COMMISSION_OPEN-CALL-PACK-.pdf?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.artdubai.ae/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/ADP_ARM-HOLDING-COMM
 ISSION_OPEN-CALL-PACK-.pdf?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
LOCATION:H Residence Sculpture Park\, Dubai\, UAE. Open to UAE-based\, regi
 onal and international artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:corridor-daisy-chain-commission-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: Corridor: DAISY CHAIN Artist Commission (Adur\, West Suss
 ex)
DESCRIPTION:Corridor seeks a socially-engaged artist based in the South Eas
 t of England working with moving image / lens-based media for DAISY CHAIN\
 , marking the 60th anniversary of Vera Chytilova's experimental film Daisi
 es (1966). The commissioned artist will work with a group of LGBTQIA+ youn
 g people aged 15-26 in Adur (West Sussex) to co-create new artworks: a 2-3
  minute moving image work and a series of 2D collage or mixed media artwor
 ks for public exhibition and screenings. DAISY CHAIN commissions six new a
 rtist moving image works overall (three England-based artists working with
  older women\, young women and LGBTQIA+ youth\; three artists in Czechia)\
 , developed in partnership with the National Film Museum in Prague (NaFilM
 ) and Brighton-based videoclub\, with results toured across England and Cz
 echia in 2027. EXPECTATIONS: devise about eight hands-on workshops incorpo
 rating film\, collage and mixed media (participants won't necessarily have
  an arts background)\; participate in 4-6 online peer sessions on collabor
 ative practice led by artist Annis Joslin\; complete exhibition-ready artw
 orks on time and to budget\; maintain a transparent dialogue on authorship
  with participants. Artists must have a participatory practice and experie
 nce of working creatively with young people. Note: to create a safe space\
 , workshops will not be publicly labelled as LGBTQIA+. FEE: GBP 4\,200 inc
 l. VAT plus travel and a materials budget. TIMELINE: shortlist notified 7 
 August\, online interviews 12 August 2026\; launch event in Adur/Worthing 
 March 2027. DEADLINE: 10am\, 3 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Corridor Proj
 ects\nLocation: Adur and Worthing\, West Sussex\, UK. Open to a socially-e
 ngaged artist based in the South East of England working with moving image
  / lens-based media.\nAward: GBP 4\,200 artist fee (inclusive of VAT) paid
  in instalments\, plus travel\, and an additional budget for materials for
  creative production\, workshops and exhibition outputs (e.g. print). No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: September 2026 to July 2027: workshops Septembe
 r-January\, post-production to February 2027\, UK and Czech tour March-Jul
 y 2027\n\nMore: https://www.corridorprojects.org.uk/daisy-chain-commission
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.corridorprojects.org.uk/daisy-chain-commission?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Adur and Worthing\, West Sussex\, UK. Open to a socially-engaged a
 rtist based in the South East of England working with moving image / lens-
 based media.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-fund-delfina-foundation-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.gith
 ub.io
DTSTAMP:20260905T174935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260827
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260828
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Delfina Foundation Residency 2027 (London
 )
DESCRIPTION:Mondriaan Fund-supported working period at London's Delfina Fou
 ndation\, one of the UK's best known artist-in-residence programmes\, hous
 ed at 29-31 Catherine Place near Buckingham Palace with space for 6 to 8 i
 nternational residents (own room\, shared kitchen and facilities). Delfina
  promotes artistic exchange and experiment\, offering visual artists and c
 urators a platform to carry out research\, develop ideas and position thei
 r practice within the global discourse\, with introductions to the London 
 art scene and Delfina's international network. The programme includes visi
 ts to museums\, galleries and non-profit platforms\, discussions with Lond
 on-based artists\, portfolio reviews with curators and regular networking 
 lunches\; residents are expected to take part. Applicants are not asked fo
 r a concrete project proposal but must submit a clear motivation: why they
  wish to take part\, what research they want to conduct\, and how it can c
 ontribute to Delfina's ongoing programme. WHO: visual artists and curators
  based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; duo appli
 cations not possible\; application must be in English. One work period ava
 ilable: 27 September to 17 December 2027. Selection by an advisory committ
 ee with a Delfina representative\; processing may exceed three months. DEA
 DLINE: Thursday 27 August 2026\, before 16:00 Dutch time / 11:00 Caribbean
  time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund / Delfina Foundation\nLocation: Lon
 don\, UK. For visual artists and curators based in the Netherlands or the 
