SUMMARY:Deadline: Scottish Documentary Institute: Bridging the Gap 2026/27
DESCRIPTION:Bridging the Gap is the Scottish Documentary Institute's flagsh
 ip short documentary talent scheme for new and emerging filmmakers based i
 n Scotland and Northern Ireland. From an initial shortlist of 12 projects\
 , up to 4 films receive full commissions with cash budgets (GBP 8\,500 per
  film in the previous round) plus production and distribution support\, wi
 th finished films distributed to cinemas and international festivals\; BtG
  shorts have a long track record of festival play and awards. The programm
 e combines professional development\, production funding and distribution:
  shortlisted filmmakers take part in intensive workshops and pitch to a pa
 nel of experts. The scheme looks for surprising\, challenging and moving s
 ubmissions that embrace the possibilities of the documentary genre and sub
 vert expectations in form and content. Access support is available for dis
 abled applicants\, and information is available in alternative formats on 
 request. Deadline: 9 September 2026\, midnight.\n\nOrganisation: Scottish 
 Documentary Institute\, with Screen Scotland and Northern Ireland Screen\n
 Location: Scotland and Northern Ireland\, UK\nAward: Up to 4 films receive
  a full commission with a cash production budget (GBP 8\,500 per film in t
 he previous round) plus production and distribution support\nDuration: 12 
 projects shortlisted for intensive workshops and a commissioning pitch\; c
 ommissioned films delivered for cinema and festival distribution\n\nMore: 
 https://www.scottishdocinstitute.com/opportunities/bridging-the-gap/?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
